#: ../../../tasks/task_types/ref.rst:2
msgid "``ref`` tasks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/ref.rst:4
msgid ""
"A ref task is essentially a call to another task. It is the default task "
"type within a sequence task, but is not often used otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/ref.rst:6
msgid ""
"A ref task can set environment variables, and pass arguments to the "
"referenced task as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/ref.rst:9
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks]\n"
"do_things.cmd = \"do_cmd\"\n"
"do_things.args = [{ name = \"things\", multiple = true, positional = "
"true }]\n"
"\n"
"do_specific_things.ref = \"do_things thing1 thing2\"\n"
"do_specific_things.env = { URGENCY = \"11\" }"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/ref.rst:19
msgid "In the above example calling:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/ref.rst:21
msgid "poe do_specific_things"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/ref.rst:25
msgid "would be equivalent to executing the following in the shell:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/ref.rst:27
msgid "URGENCY=11 do_cmd thing1 thing2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/ref.rst:33
msgid "Available task options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/ref.rst:35
msgid ""
"``ref`` tasks support all of the :doc:`standard task options <../options>` "
"with the exception of ``use_exec`` and ``executor``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/ref.rst:37
msgid "**ignore_fail** : ``bool`` :ref:`📖<Ignore reference task failure>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/ref.rst:36
msgid "bool 📖"
msgstr "bool 📖"

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/ref.rst:38
msgid ""
"If true the failure of the referenced task will be ignored and the ref task "
"will return exit code 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/ref.rst:42
msgid ""
"A ref task that references a :doc:`sequence<../task_types/sequence>` or :doc:"
"`parallel<../task_types/parallel>` task cannot use the ``capture_stdout`` "
"option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/ref.rst:46
msgid "Passing arguments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/ref.rst:48
msgid ""
"By default any arguments passed to a ref task will be forwarded to the "
"referenced task, allowing it to function as a task alias. If named arguments "
"are configured for the ref task then additional arguments can still be "
"passed to the referenced task after ``--`` on the command line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/ref.rst:50
msgid ""
"Ref tasks support parameter expansion just like cmd tasks, including the :"
"ref:`default and alternate value operators <parameter-expansion-operators>`. "
"This makes it possible to pass arguments to the referenced task "
"conditionally. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/ref.rst:52
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks.deploy]\n"
"ref = \"build ${_target:-production}\"\n"
"args = [{ name = \"_target\", positional = true, default = \"\" }]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/ref.rst:60
msgid "Ignore reference task failure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/ref.rst:62
msgid ""
"By default if the referenced task fails (has a non-zero exit code) then the "
"ref task will also fail. However it is possible to configure a ref task to "
"ignore failure using the :toml:`ignore_fail` option like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/ref.rst:64
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks.test]\n"
"test = \"pytest\"\n"
"\n"
"[tool.poe.tasks.always-pass]\n"
"ref = \"test\"\n"
"ignore_fail = true"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/ref.rst:73
msgid ""
"If the referenced task is configured to ignore failure itself then the ref "
"task will see the referenced task as having succeeded regardless of its "
"actual exit code."
msgstr ""
